      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It does appear that the era where economic efficiency unequivocally overrides national security is indeed in decline, as leaders now prioritize sovereignty as a core demand rather than a negotiable concession. However, declaring this the \"end\" of global cooperation might be premature, as the challenge now is integrating national security concerns into the fabric of international trade rather than discarding global frameworks entirely. The future likely won't be a return to 20th-century isolationism, but rather a complex, multipolar system where global treaties coexist with harder borders and more defensive globalization strategies.",
      "source": "target",
